{
 "_what_this_is": "A prompt probe on the image corpus: the model and the 32 cases held fixed, only the words of the ask varied — the experiment that decides whether the vision gap belongs to the ask or to the model.",
 "_why_they_exist": "the reading on cases.json and heldout.json left act at 9/16, and two explanations survive it: the model cannot see what an ops screenshot means, or the ask does not point it at the screenshot. calibration/provenance.md records that for the text path, rewording alone moved one model's discrimination from 0.09 to 0.77, so the question is not academic.",
 "_how_to_read_it": "Variants V1-V3 were written before any of them was run. The answer stays one word from {act, ignore} in every variant, because src/README.md line 26 requires the option to be a single token — this probes the wording of the ask, not the shape of the question.",
