 "what_the_variants_say": {
  "headline": "Wording does not close the gap. Every variant that names the screenshot scores no better at 0.600, and none beats the control's accuracy once each is allowed its own best cut.",
  "auc_rises_but_accuracy_falls": "AUC climbs from 0.891 to 0.957 while accuracy at 0.600 falls from 0.781 to 0.688: the rewording pushes the whole distribution down, improving the ordering while moving fewer act cases over a fixed bar. An AUC gain the kernel cannot spend is not a gain.",
  "best_cut_flat": "At each variant's own best cut all four land on 0.906 or below: V0 0.906, V1 0.875, V2 0.906, V3 0.906. V3 buys one more act case (14/16) by giving back one ignore case (15/16), which is a trade, not an improvement."
 },
 "the_finding_that_matters": {
  "what": "The control's 9/16 at the shipped 0.600 is not the model's ceiling on these cases. At a cut of 0.150 the same checkpoint, same prompt, same cases score 0.906 with act 13/16 and ignore still 16/16 perfect.",
  "why_the_cut_is_wrong_here": "0.600 was calibrated on text cases (docs/decisions.md row 12). On image-bearing messages the probabilities sit lower: across both halves no ignore case ever exceeds p_act 0.134, while act cases have medians of 0.616 and 0.735 and minimums of 0.095 and 0.024. The classes barely overlap — AUC 0.891 — but 0.600 slices through the middle of the act range.",
  "not_self_chosen": "The cut was not picked on the cases that then scored it: choosing it on one half and scoring the other gives 0.150 from each half independently, with cross-validated accuracy 0.906 (heldout 15/16, first 14/16).",
  "still_a_32_case_result": "Two folds of sixteen is not a calibrated operating point, and both halves are synthetic screenshots. What it establishes is where the gap lives, not what the cut should be."
 },
 "what_was_not_measured": [
  "The text path was not re-measured, so the claim that image verdicts sit lower than text ones rests on the two sets' own earlier readings (text AUC 1.000 at 0.600 on set4) rather than on a run that interleaves them.",
  "No cut for image-bearing messages is proposed here. Changing the operating point is docs/decisions.md row 12, and choosing it needs a set written for that purpose.",
  "One message with one image, rendered screenshots, 32 cases — the same limits the two reading files carry."
 ]
}